{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/references/aristotle-cli.md\nprintf '\\\\n--- MEMORY ---\\\\n'\nsed -n '42,85p' <original-home>/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md\nprintf '\\\\n--- WORKTREE ---\\\\n'\npwd\ngit status --short\nprintf '\\\\n--- TOP-LEVEL POLICY/STATE FILES ---\\\\n'\nrg --files -g 'AGENTS.md' -g 'PLAN.md' -g 'TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md' -g 'SOURCE-CONTRACT.md' -g 'CONTEXT-LEDGER.md' -g '*HANDOFF*.md' -g '*STATUS*.md' -g '*CLOSEOUT*.md' | sort\"","aggregated_output":"# Aristotle CLI reference\n\n## Setup\n\n- Install: `uv tool install aristotlelib`\n- Verify: `aristotle --version`\n- Authenticate: set `ARISTOTLE_API_KEY` in the shell environment, or use the skill wrapper `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n\nIf the key is stored near the end of `~/.bashrc`, noninteractive commands may not see it because many `.bashrc` files contain:\n\n```bash\ncase $- in\n    *i*) ;;\n      *) return;;\nesac\n```\n\nIn that case, do not rely on `source ~/.bashrc`. Use the wrapper, which reads a literal `export ARISTOTLE_API_KEY=...` assignment without printing it:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh formalize input.md\n```\n\n## Core commands\n\nSubmit a Lean project for sorry filling or proof search:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh submit \"Fill in all sorries\" --project-dir ./my-lean-project --wait\n```\n\nFormalize a TeX or paper source:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh formalize paper.tex --wait --destination output.tar.gz\n```\n\nList recent jobs:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh list --limit 10\n```\n\nDownload a completed job:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh download <project-id> --destination result.tar.gz\n```\n\nPass the key directly for one command only:\n\n```bash\naristotle submit \"My prompt\" --api-key \"$ARISTOTLE_API_KEY\" --project-dir ./my-lean-project --wait\n```\n\n## Recommended project loop\n\n1. Inspect the Lean project locally.\n2. Run the narrowest local build or test that exercises the target files.\n3. Submit a focused Aristotle prompt against the project directory.\n4. Wait for the run if the expected result is a concrete patch.\n5. Download or inspect the produced artifact.\n6. Rebuild locally and repeat with a tighter prompt if needed.\n\n## Prompt shape\n\nKeep prompts short and file-bound. Good prompts mention:\n\n- the exact project directory\n- the theorem or file to work on\n- whether to fill `sorry`s, formalize a statement, or debug a failing proof\n- what counts as a useful partial result\n\nAvoid vague prompts such as \"improve this project\" unless the scope is intentionally broad.\n\n--- MEMORY ---\n# Task Group: source-workspace two-lane Aristotle/Codex formalization autopilot\n\nscope: autonomous two-lane theorem formalization, terminal-status Codex closeout, safe artifact staging, and resource-bounded Lean verification\napplies_to: cwd=source-workspace; reuse_rule=reuse only after checking the live queues, `state.json`, systemd unit, Lean checkout, and Aristotle task state; no acceptance or advancement is implied by this partial rollout\n\n## Task 1: prepare and launch finite-fiber and stabilizer-hyperfinite queues\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-06T14-29-28-EPRR-two_lane_aristotle_autopilot_closeout_hardening.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/06/rollout-2026-08-06T16-29-28-019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-06T18:07:30+00:00, thread_id=019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677, success: two-lane queues and compact manuscript staging verified)\n\n### keywords\n\n- Aristotle, Codex, `aristotle_autopilot.py`, autopilot.toml, FF15–FF23, P37–P46, `AUTOPILOT_ACCEPTED: yes`, `AUTOPILOT_DECISION: advance`, AUTONOMY_POLICY.md\n\n## Task 2: diagnose systemd and quarantine-closeout failures\n\n### rollout_summary_files\n\n- rollout_summaries/2026-08-06T14-29-28-EPRR-two_lane_aristotle_autopilot_closeout_hardening.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/08/06/rollout-2026-08-06T16-29-28-019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-06T18:07:30+00:00, thread_id=019fd77a-ab18-78f3-a38a-968e45471677, partial: recovered closeout path; FF15/P37 advancement unverified)\n\n### keywords\n\n- systemd, `AUTOPILOT_CODEX_BIN`, `<original-home>/.nvm/versions/node/v24.14.0/bin/codex`, `[Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'codex'`, quarantine snapshot, `.lake`, `lake build`, state.json\n\n## User preferences\n\n- when the user said Aristotle may “develop necessary theory” or take “another easier route” -> permit project-local supporting theory and alternative recognizable proofs, but require explicit assumptions and no silent weakening [Task 1]\n- when the user requested copying only `main.tex` and bibliography -> stage only `manuscript/main.tex`, `manuscript/references.bib`, and `manuscript/mainNotes.bib`, not the whole Overleaf tree [Task 1]\n- when the user asked to “append the endgame packets and start the loop” -> carry theorem-target packets through the requested endgame rather than stopping at conditional infrastructure interfaces [Task 1]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n- The live runner is `work/aristotle_autopilot/aristotle_autopilot.py`, configured by `work/aristotle_autopilot/autopilot.toml`. It has independent finite-fiber FF15–FF23 and stabilizer-hyperfinite P37–P46 queues, one active Aristotle task per lane, Codex closeout only at terminal status, and advancement only after both machine-readable acceptance and decision fields. [Task 1]\n- Upload staging contains the Lean project, the three approved manuscript files, and `AUTONOMY_POLICY.md`; the policy forbids `sorry`, `admit`, axioms, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, and silent weakening. [Task 1]\n- The user systemd timer polls every five minutes. For NVM installation, the service and Python resolution need explicit `PATH` and `AUTOPILOT_CODEX_BIN=<original-home>/.nvm/versions/node/v24.14.0/bin/codex`; this run verified `codex-cli 0.146.0`. [Task 2]\n- Persist closeout metadata in `work/aristotle_autopilot/state.json` before starting Codex. An interrupted closeout without a machine-readable decision halts for review rather than retrying or advancing ambiguously. [Task 2]\n\n## Failures and how to do differently\n\n- symptom: systemd reports `[Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'codex'` and terminal Aristotle jobs never close out -> cause: the NVM executable is outside noninteractive PATH -> fix: set the absolute Codex path in both the service and runner, then verify the service environment. [Task 2]\n- symptom: a closeout consumes about 13 GB and clones/builds Mathlib -> cause: `lake build` was run in a stripped downloaded Aristotle quarantine snapshot with no `.lake` -> fix: inspect/quarantine there, copy only the reviewed candidate to the already-built live project, and run all Lean checks only in that live checkout. [Task 2]\n- status guard: at rollout end FF15 and P37 were still active. Do not claim candidate acceptance, FF15 integration, or FF16/P38 submission until `state.json`, closeout output/review, and live Lean checks agree. [Task 2]\n\n\n--- WORKTREE ---\nlean/stabilizer\n M AGENTS.md\n M Formalization.lean\n M PROGRESS.md\n M README.md\n M aristotle_tasks/TEMPLATE.md\n?? AristotleCandidates/AlgebraicLimitOperatorRepresentation.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/BicommutantNormalTransport.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/BicommutantVonNeumannCore.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/CStarAlphaGNSBridge.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/CStarCompletionAlphaInterface.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/CStarGNSBridge.lean\n?? AristotleCandidates/CStarInductiveLimitFeasibility.