{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' PLAN.md\nprintf '\\\\n--- DECISION ---\\\\n'\nsed -n '1,260p' work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md\nprintf '\\\\n--- PACKET ---\\\\n'\nsed -n '1,300p' aristotle_tasks/P48-general-lattice-projection-tower.md\nprintf '\\\\n--- PROGRESS ---\\\\n'\ntail -180 PROGRESS.md\nprintf '\\\\n--- HANDOFF/REVIEW INDEX ---\\\\n'\nfind reviews work -maxdepth 3 -type f -printf '%p\\\\n' | sort | tail -100\nprintf '\\\\n--- TASK LOG ---\\\\n'\ntail -100 history/logs/20260807T101645Z-050a4ee9-tasks.log\"","aggregated_output":"# Active plan: two-lane stabilizer-algebra formalization\n\n## Decision — 2026-08-07\n\nThe project now has two parallel mathematical targets sharing finite\nstabilizer and operator-algebra infrastructure, but neither is allowed to\nsilently supply the other one's hypotheses.\n\n### Lane G — general lattices and central type-III exclusion\n\n**Source basis:** `main.tex:332-342`, with the corner proof at\n`main.tex:1026-1536`.\n\nFor a general consistent stabilizer system and region, construct the decreasing\nlocal-code projection tower, its strong limit `q`, and the finite corner\n`q M_Gamma q`. Prove that the vector functional `tau_q` is a faithful normal\ntracial **state** on that corner, hence that `q` is finite; prove `q` is full;\nand derive that every nonzero central projection `z` has `zq != 0` finite in\n`z M_Gamma`. Conclude that no nonzero central summand is type III.\n\nThis lane does **not** require a direct-integral formalization or a global\ntrace/weight on `M_Gamma`. A global faithful normal semifinite weight is a\nseparate optional strengthening. The condition to formalize is the existence\nof a nonzero finite **projection/corner** in each nonzero central summand, not\nmerely a finite-dimensional subalgebra.\n\n### Lane H — explicit local-hyperbolic tensor-factor model\n\n**Source basis:** `main.tex:1671-1679`, `main.tex:1898-2004`.\n\nFrom a coherent local hyperbolic basis, construct the finite coordinate maps,\ntheir coherent algebraic direct-limit star equivalence, concrete C-star\nmodels, the state identity, and the product GNS tensor splitting. Then prove\nthe special regional algebra is spatially isomorphic to\n\n`B(K_pure) barTensor R_mixed`.\n\nAfter proving the two factors and their spatial tensor product, derive the\ntrivial-center/factor conclusion for this special case. This conclusion does\nnot follow merely from the word \"hyperbolic\"; it follows from the constructed\nspatial factorization.\n\n### Reconnection\n\nLane H gives an explicit factor theorem and, in the infinite-pure case, the\nconcrete faithful normal semifinite weight `Tr barTensor tau`. Lane G gives\nthe general no-central-type-III theorem. A final comparison theorem may show\nthat the Lane-H factor model satisfies the Lane-G finite-corner criterion, but\nthe two results remain logically independent.\n\n## Aristotle package sequence\n\n### Shared/central core\n\n| Packet | Lean target | Purpose and acceptance gate |\n|---|---|---|\n| P47 | `CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean` | Define center, central projections, finite projections, corners, central support, and fullness for the concrete von Neumann-algebra model. Prove only algebraic order/corner lemmas; no direct integral. |\n| P48 | `GeneralLatticeProjectionTower.lean` | Formalize the general-lattice exhaustion, local code projections, monotonicity, and the strong-limit projection `q`. If the stabilizer definitions do not imply a required limit fact, expose it as an auxiliary hypothesis. |\n| P49 | `FiniteCornerTrace.lean` | Derive finite-stage trace cyclicity and pass it to the compressed quasi-local C-star algebra. Keep finite codespace density data explicit. |\n| P50 | `NormalFaithfulCornerTrace.lean` | Extend `tau_q` to `q M_Gamma q`, prove normality and faithfulness from the exact density/commutation hypotheses used in the manuscript. |\n| P51 | `FullFiniteCornerCentralExclusion.lean` | Prove `q` finite, prove fullness, and derive `0 != z ->` a nonzero finite projection in `z M_Gamma`; define/use the project-local type-III obstruction. |\n\n### Explicit local-hyperbolic lane\n\n| Packet | Lean target | Purpose and acceptance gate |\n|---|---|---|\n| P52 | `CoherentLocalHyperbolicCoordinates.lean` | Build finite coordinate blocks and an exhaustion from local hyperbolic data. Audit whether finite support suffices; otherwise isolate the exact local-finiteness/coherence assumption. |\n| P53 | `LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha.lean` | Construct the finite stage maps, phase calibration, and coherent algebraic `alpha`; instantiate the existing direct-limit theorems without supplied stage equivalences. |\n| P54 | `UHFReferenceRepresentation.lean` | Construct a faithful compatible Hilbert/operator representation of the dyadic algebra from finite stages; do not assume an infinite tensor-product Hilbert space. |\n| P55 | `RegionalConcreteCStarAlpha.lean` | Construct source and regional closed operator-range C-star algebras and extend the P53 alpha by density. |\n| P56 | `RegionalProductStateIdentity.lean` | Prove the stabilizer/product-state equality on finite Pauli words and extend it by density and continuity. |\n| P57 | `ProductGNSTensorFactorization.lean` | Construct the pure/mixed product GNS Hilbert-space tensor splitting and the spatial represented-algebra identification. |\n| P58 | `MixedUHFHyperfiniteFactor.lean` | Construct/prove the finite mixed matrix and infinite mixed hyperfinite-II1 alternatives under project-local factor and normal-trace definitions. |\n| P59 | `LocalHyperbolicFactorTraceTheorem.lean` | Transport P57--P58 to the regional algebra, prove trivial center, and state the finite-pure trace versus infinite-pure faithful-normal-semifinite-weight dichotomy. |\n\n### Optional strengthening/reconnection\n\n| Packet | Lean target | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| P60 | `FullCornerSemifiniteWeight.lean` | Optional globalization of a full finite corner to a faithful normal semifinite weight, if needed beyond no-type-III exclusion. |\n| P61 | `HyperbolicImpliesCentralCriterion.lean` | Show the explicit Lane-H model supplies the finite-corner criterion used by Lane G. |\n\n## Initial parallel wave\n\nSubmit only the four independent foundation packets first: P47, P48, P52,\nand P54. Integrate and semantically audit them before submitting dependent\npackets. Existing P42--P46 task drafts are preserved as historical drafts;\nthey are not evidence and must be re-scoped against this plan before reuse.\n\n## Non-negotiable gates\n\n1. No claim that `q M_Gamma q` has merely a semifinite weight when the\n   construction actually targets a finite faithful normal tracial state.\n2. No claim of a global trace/weight on `M_Gamma` from the finite-corner\n   theorem alone.\n3. No claim that a finite-dimensional subalgebra excludes type III; the proof\n   must produce a nonzero finite projection in every nonzero central summand.\n4. No claim that hyperbolic data imply a factor before the spatial tensor\n   factorization and factorhood of both factors are proved.\n5. Every manuscript-facing packet identifies an exact `main.tex` locator and\n   every extra analytic hypothesis appears as a named field, never an axiom.\n\n---\n\n# Previous single-lane plan: retained background\n\n## Objective\n\nFormalize, from the manuscript's actual finite-support adapted-coordinate data,\na state-preserving C-star isomorphism from the quasi-local Pauli algebra to the\nregional algebra.  Obtain the represented von Neumann algebra equivalence by\nthe canonical GNS unitary, then apply an independently established product\nfactor classification.\n\nThe source basis is exclusively `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md` and the cited manuscript\nlocators.  In particular, no gLU/refinement/layer-coherence premise is allowed\nunless later added explicitly as a new auxiliary assumption.\n\n## Current position\n\nThe project already has checked conditional interfaces for:\n\n1. finite Pauli/stabilizer coordinates and pure/mixed states;\n2. algebraic direct limits, their induced algebraic equivalence `alpha`, and\n   compatible state transport;\n3. supplied C-star completions and a supplied C-star extension of `alpha`;\n4. GNS transport for supplied compatible C-star states; and\n5. supplied normal/product-factor transport.\n\nThese are scaffolding.  They do not discharge the manuscript-specific finite\ncoordinate construction or the product-factor classification.\n\n## Phase A — exact finite coordinate theorem\n\n**Goal:** Replace abstract finite-stage star equivalences by maps constructed\nfrom a finite restriction of the adapted symplectic basis.\n\n1. Specify a finite region/exhaustion and the finite Pauli label spaces.\n2. Define the coordinate map from the adapted `z_i,x_i` data.\n3. Prove the Pauli multiplier and star equations, including the required phase\n   correction.\n4. Prove the map is a finite-stage complex star-algebra equivalence.\n5. Prove its stabilizer membership criterion and the finite product-state\n   expectation formula.\n\n**Gate A:** no supplied finite-stage star equivalence remains in the finite\nmanuscript theorem; only explicitly stated finite adapted-coordinate data does.\n\n## Phase B — coherence and quasi-local C-star isomorphism\n\n**Goal:** Construct the actual C-star isomorphism `alpha`, rather than assume\nan algebraic or completed extension.\n\n1. Prove the Phase-A maps commute exactly with all finite-region inclusions.\n2. Form the algebraic direct-limit star equivalence.\n3. Specify the quasi-local C-star completions as inductive-limit completions.\n4. Prove the algebraic map is isometric on the dense quasi-local subalgebras.\n5. Extend it uniquely to a C-star star-algebra equivalence\n   `alpha : P_quasilocal ≃⋆ₐ[ℂ] A_regional`.\n\n**Gate B:** P23 and P25 are instantiated by proved data, not used as supplied\ninterfaces.\n\n## Phase C — state identity and GNS transport\n\n**Goal:** Prove the regional state pulled back by `alpha` is the pure/mixed\nproduct state.\n\n1. Check equality on finite Pauli-word bases using Phase A's stabilizer\ncriterion.\n2. Prove compatibility under inclusions and hence equality on the quasi-local\nC-star algebra by density/continuity.\n3. Instantiate the existing C-star/GNS bridge to obtain the canonical GNS\nunitary and its intertwining identity.\n4. Use conjugation by that unitary to identify the represented von Neumann\nalgebras.\n\n**Gate C:** do not use a separate quasi-equivalence/normal-folium argument.\nIt is unnecessary once the state-preserving C-star isomorphism is proved.\n\n## Phase D — product representation classification\n\n**Goal:** Independently prove or source the product-state representation\ntheorem.\n\n1. Split coordinate indices into pure and mixed sectors.\n2. Establish the infinite-product GNS factorization.\n3. Identify the pure sector as `B(K_pure)`.\n4. Identify the mixed sector as a finite matrix factor when finite, or the\nhyperfinite `II_1` factor when infinite.\n5. Establish the spatial tensor-product identification of the product\nrepresentation.\n\n**Gate D:** every analytic theorem is either formalized against a supported\nMathlib API or recorded as an exact external theorem with source locator and\nexplicit hypothesis.\n\n## Phase E — theorem and trace corollaries\n\n1. Transport the Phase-D product classification through the Phase-C GNS\nunitary to the regional von Neumann algebra.\n2. State the finite-pure and infinite-pure cases separately.\n3. Finite pure sector: derive the normalized tracial-state conclusion.\n4. Infinite pure sector: state the faithful normal semifinite trace/weight\nconclusion; do not call it a tracial state.\n5. Audit every conclusion against `main.tex:1740-1752` and record any required\nmanuscript correction separately.\n\n## Parallelization\n\nUntil Phase B is blocked on a single coherent-coordinate construction, run in\nparallel:\n\n- finite phase/cocycle verification;\n- finite adapted-coordinate/stabilizer-state verification;\n- finite inclusion/coherence lemmas;\n- Mathlib/API feasibility audits for C-star inductive limits and GNS products;\n- product mixed-sector classification/source work.\n\nDo not parallelize mutually dependent attempts at the same global `alpha`.\nEach new Aristotle packet must use `aristotle_tasks/TEMPLATE.md` and state its\nsource basis plus every auxiliary assumption.\n\n## Exit criterion\n\nCall the manuscript theorem formally established only when Gates A--D are\ndischarged and Phase E compiles without substituting supplied interfaces for\nthe central finite-coordinate, C-star-extension, state-identity, or\nproduct-classification claims.\n\n--- DECISION ---\n# Two-lane formalization decision\n\nDate: 2026-08-07\n\nThe active Codex/Aristotle loop follows the two-lane plan in `PLAN.md`.\n\n**Lane G** formalizes the manuscript's general-lattice corner argument:\nthe strong-limit code projection `q`, the faithful normal finite tracial state\non `q M_Gamma q`, finiteness and fullness of `q`, and the conclusion that each\nnonzero central summand has a nonzero finite projection and hence is not type\nIII. This route does not use a direct integral and does not require a global\ntrace/weight on `M_Gamma`.\n\n**Lane H** formalizes the explicit short-range/local-hyperbolic model:\ncoherent coordinate maps, an algebraic and C-star `alpha`, the product-state\nidentity, product GNS tensor factorization, and the resulting factor and\ntrace/weight classification.\n\nThe lanes meet only after their own gates are met. In particular, the explicit\ntensor-factor result proves trivial center in the special local-hyperbolic\ncase, whereas the general corner result rules out type-III central summands\nwithout asserting trivial center.\n\nThe first approved parallel Aristotle wave is P47, P48, P52, and P54. No\ndependent packet should be submitted before its prerequisite results are\nintegrated and semantically audited.\n\n--- PACKET ---\n# P48 — general-lattice local-code projection tower\n\n## Context declaration\n\n- **Source basis:** `main.tex:1026-1195`.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** `P48`; Lane `G`.\n- **Predecessors:** none.\n- **Gate discharged:** construct the decreasing local-code projections and\n  expose the exact data needed to obtain their limiting projection `q`.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** no trace on the corner, no faithfulness,\n  finiteness, fullness, global weight, or type-III conclusion.\n\nRead `PLAN.md` and `work/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md` before editing.\n\n## Mathematical target\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/GeneralLatticeProjectionTower.lean`. Formalize\na general countable lattice exhaustion, the finite stabilizer constraints seen\nat each stage, the corresponding local-code projections, and their decreasing\norder relation. Construct the strong-limit projection `q` using supported\nMathlib APIs if possible. If the pinned library cannot express or prove the\nmonotone strong limit, isolate precisely that analytic step as a named\nstructure field and prove all consequences that follow from it. The result\nmust not assume a hyperbolic basis or tensor-factor coordinates.\n\n## Auxiliary assumptions\n\nList every needed exhaustion, local finiteness, representation, convergence,\nor limit-projection hypothesis explicitly. The manuscript-facing result is\nconditional whenever such a field is not derived from the cited source data.\n\n## Files and imports\n\nCreate only `AristotleCandidates/GeneralLatticeProjectionTower.lean`. Reuse the\nfinite stabilizer/projector modules and pinned operator APIs; do not import a\nlater P47--P61 packet.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.GeneralLatticeProjectionTower` succeeds.\n- The exact Lean declaration representing `q` and every convergence premise is\n  reported.\n- No placeholder or hidden analytic assumption is introduced.\n- The result stays in Lane G and makes none of the forbidden conclusions.\n\n--- PROGRESS ---\n  supported X/Z coordinate labels and maps the singleton coordinate labels to\n  the chosen basis vectors.\n- ASC-001 — for a selected set of Z coordinates, Lean now identifies the\n  corresponding coordinate subspace both as the span of those Z basis\n  vectors and as the finite words with no X coordinate and no Z coordinate\n  outside the selected set.  This is the exact linear selection criterion\n  required before comparing the regional stabilizer state with the\n  pure/mixed product state.\n- FQS-001 — Lean now reads the recursive finite-qubit Pauli label as its\n  finite X/Z coordinate list and proves that the pure/mixed product-state\n  indicator is exactly the selected-Z condition: a pure coordinate has no X\n  exponent, and a mixed coordinate is the identity label.  Under an arbitrary\n  supplied adapted coordinate basis, that condition is literal membership in\n  the selected-Z stabilizer submodule.  The coherent direct-limit state theorem\n  has a corresponding selected-Z indicator form on source basis words.\n- `PCC-001` — a phase-corrected additive map of Pauli labels respects word\n  multiplication and star exactly when it satisfies explicit multiplier and\n  involution equations.  This isolates the cocycle data that symplecticity\n  alone does not supply.  The cross-algebra word-basis extension is now also\n  checked: its two compatibility equations and a specified Pauli-word basis\n  yield a genuine `StarAlgEquiv`.\n- `SCC-001` — the quotient of two multiplier phases is an additive character,\n  calibrating by an additive character preserves the multiplier equation, and\n  every additive character on a vector subspace extends to the ambient vector\n  space along a complementary subspace.  This is the exact algebraic\n  stabilizer-sign calibration: the finite-field character is self-conjugate,\n  and calibration preserves both Pauli-word compatibility equations.  The\n  concrete finite-support quadratic phase is now independently formalized;\n  relating it to the actual regional stabilizer convention remains separate.\n- QPR-001 — the explicit ZMod 4 finite-support quadratic refinement has its\n  polarization and diagonal identities fully checked.  Its discrepancy pairing\n  is additive in both words, symmetric for a symmetric discrepancy, and has\n  additive order two.  These facts instantiate the cross-algebra Pauli-word\n  multiplication and involution certificates and, with a supplied word-basis\n  linear equivalence, a `StarAlgEquiv`.\n- QPT-001 — the concrete finite-support phase theorem now composes that\n  `StarAlgEquiv` with the finite-pure times qubit-UHF trace transport: whenever\n  the regional Pauli-word exponents, involution phases, and word-basis map are\n  supplied, Lean constructs both the star-algebra equivalence and its induced\n  algebraic tracial state with the elementary-tensor product formula.  The\n  Pauli-word interface has been weakened from `Ring` to `Semiring`, the exact\n  structure carried by the concrete algebraic UHF direct limit.\n- PTO-001 — two isometries whose range projections sum to the identity rule\n  out even an algebraic unital cyclic trace.  This is the checked obstruction\n  behind the infinite-pure-sector case; the tracial-state theorem is therefore\n  deliberately limited to a finite pure matrix factor.\n- ALT-001 — compatible finite-stage `StarAlgEquiv`s and compatible target\n  algebraic tracial states induce a source-side algebraic tracial state on the\n  corresponding quasi-local direct limit.  The theorem evaluates it exactly\n  on every finite-stage representative.  The concrete finite-pure UHF trace\n  now has the matching finite-stage elementary-tensor formula.\n- FQP-001 — every finite stage of the dyadic qubit tower now has an explicit\n  ordered Pauli-word `StarSystem` and a complex Pauli-word basis.  The\n  identity-qubit embeddings preserve its words, basis vectors, multiplication\n  multipliers, and star multipliers under coherent label maps.  Thus the UHF\n  target-side finite-stage word hypotheses are no longer abstract assumptions;\n  assembling them into one global target word system remains open.\n- PMS-001 — for every Boolean sequence specifying whether each newly adjoined\n  qubit is pure or maximally mixed, the corresponding finite product\n  functionals are algebraic states, are compatible with all dyadic embeddings,\n  and induce an algebraic state on the UHF direct limit.  Their values on every\n  finite Pauli word are proved recursively: pure coordinates permit only zero\n  X exponent, while mixed coordinates permit only the identity word.  The\n  all-mixed specialization is proved equal to the previously checked UHF\n  tracial state.  Lean also proves that even the one-qubit pure specialization\n  is not cyclic and hence not an algebraic tracial state.\n- PTR-001 — this nontraciality is now proved at arbitrary finite and\n  direct-limit coordinates: if any Boolean coordinate is pure, explicit\n  matrix units witness a failure of cyclicity.  Consequently the algebraic\n  UHF product state is tracial if and only if every coordinate is maximally\n  mixed, in which case it is the checked UHF trace.\n- CBL-001 — finite-stage star-algebra equivalences need not be assumed\n  coherent on every algebra element: if the source connecting maps, target\n  vectors, and coordinate maps agree on a specified source basis, Lean proves\n  the full commuting square by linear-basis extensionality.\n- CPS-001 — a phase-corrected finite coordinate system now has a concrete\n  direct-limit state interface.  Coherent source basis transport, phases, and\n  finite Pauli labels imply full-stage equivalence coherence and hence a\n  star-algebra equivalence to the algebraic qubit-UHF direct limit; the induced\n  source state evaluates a basis word as its phase times the pure/mixed Pauli\n  selection indicator.  The all-mixed specialization pulls the UHF trace back\n  to a source algebraic tracial state; more generally its pure/mixed pullback\n  is tracial exactly when every coordinate is mixed.  Constructing the\n  regional inputs remains open.\n- ACS-001 — if supplied finite-stage regional data identify selected target\n  Z-coordinates with the actual source stabilizer words, Lean derives the\n  exact phase-calibrated stabilizer expectation formula on every source basis word.\n  The stronger form states that hypothesis as literal membership in the\n  selected-Z submodule of an adapted coordinate basis.  Thus the remaining\n  geometric work is isolated to constructing and coherently transporting that\n  coordinate data from a separately supplied finite-coordinate realization,\n  rather than to a hidden infinite-algebra assumption. The manuscript does not\n  presently supply that realization; see `SOURCE-CONTRACT.md`.\n- ALS-001 — compatible finite-stage star-algebra equivalences transport\n  compatible algebraic states (not only tracial states) to a quasi-local\n  algebraic direct limit.  This is the exact state-level interface required by\n  a coherent regional stabilizer-coordinate construction.\n- WBE-001 — if Pauli words form a complex linear basis, checking a\n  complex-linear map on every pair of basis words proves multiplicativity on\n  all finite sums.  The corresponding conjugate-linear basis argument proves\n  star preservation; a bijective unital map satisfying both checks is packaged\n  as a star-algebra equivalence.\n- ALC-001 — a compatible family of finite-stage star-algebra maps induces a\n  star-algebra map from the algebraic directed limit.  Compatible finite-stage\n  star-algebra equivalences induce a star-algebra equivalence of the two\n  algebraic limits.  The C-star norm extension remains open.\n- CSE-001 — once a source and target are supplied as complex C-star algebras,\n  Lean proves that every complex `StarAlgEquiv` is isometric and therefore\n  continuous with continuous inverse.  A continuous target functional pulls\n  back continuously along it.  This does not construct C-star norms or\n  completions for the algebraic direct-limit models.\n- CCF-001 — the pinned Mathlib supports the finite dyadic stages as genuine\n  C-star algebras and supports closure/minimality once an ambient C-star\n  algebra is supplied.  It does not provide the C-star inductive-limit\n  construction for the algebraic dyadic limit; this is recorded as an\n  explicit missing API rather than hidden behind an axiom.\n- NMC-001 — supplied finite C-star realizations of the coherent coordinate\n  maps are isometric and continuous, and the commuting inclusion squares\n  preserve the norm estimates.  The resulting dense-subalgebra estimate is\n  exactly the analytic input needed before extending the algebraic map to a\n  completion; no completion is constructed here.\n- BMC-001 — for a star subalgebra of bounded operators on a Hilbert space,\n  Lean now constructs the algebraic bicommutant as a concrete\n  `VonNeumannAlgebra`, with monotonicity, minimality, membership, and\n  idempotence lemmas.  The analytic strong/weak double-commutant theorem is\n  still explicitly absent from the pinned Mathlib and remains separate.\n- CCC-001 — from an explicitly supplied isometric star representation of a\n  pre-C-star algebra into bounded operators, Lean constructs the closed\n  operator-range C-star algebra, its isometric dense embedding, and the\n  uniqueness equivalence between two such concrete completions.  The faithful\n  operator representation of the project-specific algebraic limit is still a\n  separate obligation.\n\n## The exact theorem still to prove\n\nThe Overleaf short-range theorem asserts a regional von Neumann algebra\nisomorphism to a type-I factor tensor a hyperfinite type-II1 factor.  It is\nnot yet formalized as a theorem because the supplied manuscript proof leaves\nthe following essential premises open:\n\n1. a finite-support adapted symplectic coordinate map whose finite-stage\n   source bases, phase correction, and target Pauli labels are coherent along\n   an exhaustion;\n2. identification of the actual regional Pauli multiplier and involution\n   exponents with the finite-support coordinate discrepancy, followed by\n   calibration to the actual stabilizer character;\n3. the induced quasi-local C-star isomorphism;\n4. factorization of the regional state into pure and normalized-tracial\n   coordinate states; and\n5. a normal/spatial extension to the respective bicommutants.\n\nThe current pinned mathlib version includes preliminary abstract and concrete\nvon Neumann-algebra definitions, but lacks a finished API for infinite von\nNeumann tensor products, normal states/traces, hyperfiniteness, and factor\nclassification.  The project therefore does not introduce any axiom for the\ntarget theorem.\n\n## Last verification\n\n```text\nlake build\nlake build Formalization.AlgebraicLimitStateTransport Formalization.QubitMatrixState Formalization.FinitePureMixedQubitState Formalization\nlake build Formalization.TraceTransport Formalization\nlake build Formalization.CoherentBasisEquiv Formalization.CoherentPhaseQubitState Formalization\nlake build Formalization.PureCoordinateNotTracial Formalization\nlake build Formalization.AdaptedStabilizerSubspace Formalization\nlake build Formalization.FiniteQubitPauliSelection Formalization.CoherentPhaseQubitState Formalization\nlake build Formalization.CStarEquivExtension Formalization\nlake build AristotleCandidates.CStarInductiveLimitFeasibility AristotleCandidates.FiniteCoordinateMapNormControl\nlake env lean /tmp/stabilizer_hyperfinite_axioms_run4.lean\npdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error .../001-tensor-product-trace.tex\n```\n\nLean reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound` for the\nchecked tensor-amplification, concrete dyadic direct-limit trace,\nfinite-support quadratic-phase, induced-trace, finite-qubit Pauli-word,\npure/mixed product-state, basis-level coherence, phase-corrected direct-limit\nequivalence/state transport, and properly-infinite trace-obstruction theorems.\nNo source theorem contains `sorry`, `admit`, or a user-declared axiom.  The\nblueprint build output is kept under `/tmp`, not in this source project.\n\n--- HANDOFF/REVIEW INDEX ---\nreviews/P37-algebraic-limit-operator-representation-closeout.md\nreviews/P38-concrete-quasilocal-cstar-model-closeout.md\nreviews/P39-state-preserving-gns-model-closeout.md\nreviews/P40-bicommutant-normal-transport-closeout.md\nreviews/P41-product-factor-classification-boundary-closeout.md\nreviews/P47-center-finite-projection-core-closeout.md\nwork/FORMALIZATION-AUDIT-DECISION.md\nwork/FORMALIZATION-SEMANTIC-AUDIT.md\nwork/TWO-LANE-FORMALIZATION-DECISION.md\n\n--- TASK LOG ---\nID                                   CREATED              NAME                           STATUS         \n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\neb6f0455-37d3-4897-94fe-3a43c0425b0e 43 mins ago          # Autonomous proof-developm... COMPLETE       \n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
